screens.body:
A media query is CSS with a condition: "only apply these rules when the screen is at least this wide."

@media (min-width: 768px) { ... } means "on tablets and bigger, do this." Everything inside the braces is normal CSS.

min-width = "this wide and up". max-width = "this wide and down". Mobile-first designs mostly use min-width.

code.snippet:
img {
  max-width: 100%; /* shrink to fit, never overflow */
  height: auto;
}
